@* ============================================================
   PHASE 11 — STATIC OIL-BATH ENGINE · DYNAMO IDLE BOOTSTRAP
   Deep Indigo (#1a0050 / #0d0028) + Volt Green (#39FF14 / #00cc00)
   CORRECTED ARCHITECTURE from Phase 10:
     · Engine = PISTON-LESS static sealed oil-bath mechanical unit
     · Generator (custom low/high gear) mounts ON TOP of static engine
     · 2 Rails + 3 Wheels per side → input torque to static engine
     · Only 2 pistons exist — near the rear water/boiler tank
     · Radiator + Alternator on LEFT side
     · Dynamo attachment concept for DC idle bootstrap
   Scientific target: sustain the loop at IDLE via Dynamo assist
   Phase 12 will refine geometry after bench observation
   ============================================================ *@

<!-- =====================================================
     PHASE 11 BANNER
     ===================================================== -->
<div class="p11-banner">
    <div class="p11-phase-pill">Phase 11 · Static Oil-Bath Engine + Dynamo Idle Bootstrap</div>
    <h1>Piston-Less <em>Static Mechanical Engine — Corrected Architecture</em></h1>
    <p>
        Phase 11 corrects the engine concept from Phase 10. There are <strong>no pistons inside the engine block</strong>.
        The core unit is a sealed, oil-bathed static mechanical transmission — think of it as a static gearbox
        whose internal rotating members are driven by the two steam rails and three wheels on each side.
        The custom generator (with selectable low/high gear) sits directly on top and harvests that rotation.
        Only two pistons exist in the entire system, located near the rear water/boiler tank, producing the
        steam-pressure impulse that drives the rails. A Dynamo attachment concept is introduced to provide
        initial direct current at idle, solving the cold-start self-sustain gap identified in Phase 10.
    </p>
</div>

<!-- =====================================================
     ARCHITECTURE CORRECTION CALLOUT
     ===================================================== -->
<div class="p11-section">

    <div class="p11-section-label">Phase 11 · Architecture Correction from Phase 10</div>
    <h2 class="p11-section-title">What changed — and why</h2>

    <div class="p11-correction-grid">
        <div class="p11-corr-card p11-corr-wrong">
            <div class="p11-corr-badge">Phase 10 — Incorrect Assumption</div>
            <ul class="p11-corr-list">
                <li>Engine assumed to contain pistons driving wheels directly</li>
                <li>Generator coupling to "oil pan" was ambiguous</li>
                <li>"Oil pan" treated as a secondary part, not the engine itself</li>
                <li>6 pistons distributed across two piston rails inside the engine</li>
                <li>Torque path from piston → crank → wheel was standard IC layout</li>
                <li>Throttle valve assumed to control pistons inside main block</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="p11-corr-card p11-corr-right">
            <div class="p11-corr-badge p11-corr-badge-right">Phase 11 — Corrected Design</div>
            <ul class="p11-corr-list">
                <li>Engine = sealed oil-bath static mechanical unit (piston-less)</li>
                <li>Internal rotating members driven by 2 rails + 3 wheels per side</li>
                <li>Generator mounts ON TOP — direct shaft coupling to internal rotors</li>
                <li>Only 2 pistons, located at rear near the boiler/water tank</li>
                <li>Pistons produce steam impulse to rails — not to wheels directly</li>
                <li>Throttle controls the 2 rear pistons' steam admission only</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

